UID:10009255-1787684400-1787688000@catonsvillepres.org
SUMMARY:Adult Education: Reconciliation: Overcoming Obstacles and Facilitating Resolutions
DESCRIPTION:Reconciliation: Overcoming Obstacles and Facilitating Resolutions | Led by Dr. Ralph Surette\nHow can deep conflicts between us be resolved peacefully? Why can’t we discuss it? Psychological and emotional dynamics involved in both political and personal struggles can impede the reconciliation of differences. This presentation examines polarization\, anger\, blaming\, prejudice\, and forgiveness. We will explore how the process of reconciliation must include a cessation of mutual hostility\, both sides agreeing to learn more about their respective difference and a willingness to reach an accord while creating a mutual narrative that could provide a new vision of what each side aspires to realize and achieve. Join us as we explore practical approaches to overcoming conflict\, fostering understanding\, and building pathways toward reconciliation.
URL:https://catonsvillepres.org/event/adult-education-reconciliation-overcoming-obstacles-and-facilitating-resolutions/
LOCATION:Library
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://catonsvillepres.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/Bearwalk_CPC_10.18__259.jpg
END:VEVENT
